steps to deploy a php website on aws (ec2)

 - Launch the ec2 instance 
 - connect through putty
 - cmd : (if you are using ubuntu just login as "ubuntu" if amzn linux "ec2-user")
 - cmd : sudo apt update (//can also us sudo apt upgrade)
 - cmd : apt install apache2 -y (installs the webserver)
 - cmd : service apache2 start (//starts the server)
 - cmd : service apache2 status (//gives the status ,  you can go the public ip and review the home page)
 - assuming that you are in home directory (i.e /home/ubuntu/)
 - cmd : cd /var/www/html/ (the default path apache2)
 - cmd : ls (the eg index file will be there , just remove it with , cmd : rm index.html)
 - cmd : apt install php
 ---------------------------------------------------------

 <through file zillla copy the required folder from local machine to the ec2 server>

 - Folder will be in "/home/ubuntu"

 # gotta move this to the "/var/www/html/" path so ,

 - cmd : mv folder_name /var/www/html/ (eg , mv basic /var/www/html)
 - cmd : cd /etc/apache2/sites-available/
 - cmd : ls (you'd get two .conf files)
 - cmd : nano "the first config file"
 # enter inside the config file and put the name of of your folder in them
 - cmd : service apache2 restart (//restarts the apache)
 - cmd : service apache2 status 
 ---------------------------------------------------------------
 
 refresh the page the website will be live
